# Isaac smoke PhysX monitoring and console log keys

## PhysX fail-closed (do not drop between revisions)

- Headless **and GUI** multi-target / Phase 7.5 playback smokes must subscribe
  to PhysX contact reports (`TipBodyContactMonitor` / equivalent) for the
  entire episode motion.
- Enable PhysX articulation **self-collisions** and apply
  `PhysxContactReportAPI` on robot collision prims before playback; otherwise
  robot–robot contacts are invisible to the monitor. Prepared MyCobot USD
  must keep `physxArticulation:enabledSelfCollisions=1`,
  `newton:selfCollisionEnabled=1`, and contact reports on arm `*_1`
  collision meshes (instance proxies). Link-name classification must use the
  deepest canonical link (`joint2`…`joint6_flange`), never only `g_base`.
- **Prohibited body–target contact** fails the episode (`body_contact`) and
  must fail suite acceptance when `failed_episodes > max_failed_episodes`.
- **Prohibited robot self-collision** (non-adjacent links; adjacent pairs
  follow the robot YAML `self_collision_ignore` map) fails the episode
  (`self_collision`) and **always** fails the smoke exit code — not waived by
  `max_failed_episodes`.
- Tip/body/self contact evidence must be printed on the **streamed smoke
  console (stdout)** with the normative tag `phase7_2_physx:` (not only Kit UI
  messages). Absence of these lines when contacts occur is a defect.
- Kit/PhysX engine overlap or collide errors (including spawn-time
  penetrating statics from stale prims) must fail the smoke when detected;
  do not treat them as ignorable Kit noise.
- Never weaken, skip, or comment out PhysX fail-closed checks to obtain a
  green GUI/headless run.

## Inter-episode target field clear

- Each episode’s incremental (or fixed) field is planned from a **clear
  field**. Before spawning an episode’s targets — and before each
  `--no-auto-exit` replay pass — remove **all** prims under
  `/World/Phase7_2/Targets`, not only the next episode’s target ids.
  Disjoint candidate ids across episodes make partial clears leave
  overlapping cubes and silent PhysX collisions.

## Post-episode PhysX acceptance (Phase 7.5)

- After each incremental episode is populated/planned, the **host plan
  pipeline** must headless-PhysX-smoke that episode before keeping it.
  Hard PhysX errors discard and regenerate (deterministic seed advance)
  up to `max_physx_regenerations`; exhaustion fails closed.
- Discard diagnostics must support later **sphere-cover** fixes: category,
  canonical link pair (or body↔target), leg ids, waypoint/`q_rad`, and
  when evaluable host-side sphere clearance. Tag: `phase7_5_physx_regen:`.
  See `spec.md` §8 Phase 7.5 and `docs/console_log_keys.md`.
- PhysX stays host-only; do not import PhysX into core `mycobot_curobo`.

## Console log glossary

- Canonical key meanings live in [`docs/console_log_keys.md`](../../docs/console_log_keys.md).
- **Whenever** console tags, `key=value` tokens, or report JSON fields are
  added, renamed, removed, or change meaning, update that glossary in the
  **same change set**, plus `CHANGES.md` and the applicable phase report /
  `spec.md` when the tag is normative.
- Prefer stable tag prefixes (`phase7_2_playback:`, `phase7_2_physx:`,
  `phase7_5_populate:`, `phase7_5_physx_regen:`, …) over ad-hoc unmarked
  prints for smoke-critical evidence.
